WEBVTT

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:20.040
Rental Magica

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:13.820
Ow, ow, ow...

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:16.090
I told you not to be so shocked.

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:18.920
Itsuki, are you okay?

00:02:19.330 --> 00:02:21.500
Kuroha... You just popped out so quickly.

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:23.540
Well, I am a ghost, after all.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:25.310
Ow! Ow! Ow!

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:27.240
Oh, dear! Is this where it hurts?

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.440
Oh, you're getting a bump now.

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:35.020
Um, nothing! I'm fine! Really!

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:35.980
What are you doing?
Um, nothing! I'm fine! Really!

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:36.420
What are you doing?

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:40.620
W-What?

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.080
Your card case.

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:42.780
Huh?

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:43.660
Behind you.

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:46.150
You dropped your business card
case when you hit your head before.

00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:47.150
Oh!

00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:00.730
"Fetish purveyor company Trismegistos"?

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:04.580
Yes. I'm Diana, the managing director.

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:09.580
Episode 11
THE FLOWER THAT
BLOOMS ON THE DEAD

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:14.890
I came to call on you as soon as I heard
Astral had reopened for business.

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:21.190
It's so hot! I wish we had an air conditioner.

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:23.090
What are you doing?

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:25.330
Practicing my poltergeist skills.

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:27.760
I thought I'd try serving coffee to our guest.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.710
So, the former President
Tsukasa had a relationship...

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:34.610
...with your company before I joined, huh?

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:38.270
Yes. From spirit paper for
talismans to purified crystal,

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:41.020
from mandrake root to fresh griffin liver,

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:43.250
we procured all sorts of things for him.

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:49.090
You look just like Tsukasa
did when he was young.

00:03:49.090 --> 00:03:50.560
Oh? Do I?

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:52.350
The resemblance is strong.

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:55.530
Hang in there, Big Sister Kuroha!

00:03:56.730 --> 00:03:58.060
Did you come here on business today?

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:00.790
No, I came to ask a favor of you.

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:04.230
The truth is, I'd like you
to harvest a flower for me.

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:05.070
A flower?

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:10.670
Caterpillar fungus.

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:17.790
Um, it's not used for herbal medicine, is it?

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:20.990
Of course not. Literally "Winter
Worm Summer Grass" in Japanese,

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:24.430
as the name implies, it parasitically
grows on worms and such in wintertime,

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:26.260
and then it becomes grass in summer.

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:28.820
The name is a generic term for
over 300 varieties of mushroom.

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:32.160
Mushroom? But that photo
shows a flower blooming.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:34.460
Which is what makes it a fetish.

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:38.540
It shares its name with caterpillar fungus,
but it's a completely different thing.

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:42.580
A magical bloom, sprouting an unlikely flower
feeding off nutrients that shouldn't exist.

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:44.670
You know quite a lot about it.

00:04:45.810 --> 00:04:48.250
This particular one attaches itself to people.

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:49.120
To people?

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:51.090
Yes, it lives off of people.

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:54.980
Years need to pass before it blooms
on the skeleton of the host.

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:57.220
An extremely dangerous fetish.

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:00.820
On the other hand, it doesn't change
anything until the host dies.

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:05.830
It does leech a bit of the human
host's life force, but only faintly.

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:07.130
Um...

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:08.030
What?

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:13.300
Did the host of the caterpillar
fungus know about it?

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:16.740
Oh, are you asking if I infected the
host without them knowing?

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:17.730
No, just...

00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:22.220
They knew. We discussed the whole
thing before making our contract.

00:05:22.850 --> 00:05:26.150
Even so, growing a flower on a human being!

00:05:26.390 --> 00:05:29.580
That's what makes it so valuable.

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:33.720
Only one can grow on a person,
and it blooms only once in a lifetime.

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:38.700
And you... sell... such precious flowers?

00:05:38.970 --> 00:05:40.760
That's my job.

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:41.900
Your job?!

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:44.300
It's a normal job in the world of mages.

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:46.970
Boss, you have to start getting used to that.

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:50.380
Will you take the job?

00:05:50.510 --> 00:05:51.670
I'm not sure.

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:55.370
Wouldn't this job be more
up Trismegistos's alley?

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:58.750
If you're worried about compensation,
we'll pay any price you ask.

00:05:58.850 --> 00:05:59.620
Seriously?!

00:05:59.890 --> 00:06:03.150
Brother Pres, take it! Buy us an A/C!

00:06:03.890 --> 00:06:05.320
I couldn't do it...

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:08.990
Tsukasa promised me that he
would handle this matter.

00:06:09.230 --> 00:06:10.060
My father did?

00:06:10.230 --> 00:06:14.900
Yes. Ten years ago, when the person the
caterpillar fungus was implanted in died,

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:16.670
Tsukasa made me a promise.

00:06:17.070 --> 00:06:21.870
That the person's burial and the picking of the
flower would be handled by his people at Astral.

00:06:22.010 --> 00:06:24.140
So, this is a job my father accepted.

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:31.650
The caterpillar fungus blooms tomorrow night.

00:06:32.920 --> 00:06:33.650
Tomorrow?

00:06:35.820 --> 00:06:37.260
Ow, ow, ow...

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:40.320
We should put some ice
on that when we get back.

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:41.050
Yeah.

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:43.460
There's something else going on here.

00:06:43.660 --> 00:06:47.460
She wouldn't have come to us if
this was just to pick a flower.

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:52.070
She's definitely hiding something.
We have to be ready.

00:06:54.340 --> 00:06:57.440
I wonder what sort of promise
Dad made to Diana?

00:06:58.450 --> 00:07:00.940
Maybe Nekoyashiki knows something about it.

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:04.810
10 years ago, even he would
have been a total newbie.

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:06.950
I doubt he'd know the full circumstances.

00:07:07.050 --> 00:07:09.690
Anyway, he's been shut up in his room
like spam in a can since yesterday...

00:07:09.690 --> 00:07:12.180
...working on his serialized story,
so we can't contact him.

00:07:12.790 --> 00:07:15.490
Anyway, we should get the flower and go home.

00:07:17.130 --> 00:07:18.330
A crescent moon, huh?

00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:20.460
My power will be a little weak.

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:22.530
I'll go from the air.

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:25.270
If anything happens, it'll be easy for me to move.

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:25.930
Right.

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:35.180
Are you thinking about your father?

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:36.910
Yeah. A little.

00:07:37.450 --> 00:07:39.150
He looked like you?

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:44.090
I don't really remember. I hardly ever saw him.

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:47.460
I see. I wonder what he was like.

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:50.360
Itsuki?!

00:07:52.930 --> 00:07:54.870
I found it! The caterpillar fungus!

00:07:58.470 --> 00:07:59.340
The flower!

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:06.600
It's bloomed.

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:13.480
Kuroha?!

00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:18.250
Boss!

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:26.290
It's bloomed, at last.

00:08:40.820 --> 00:08:42.010
What's this mist?

00:08:46.950 --> 00:08:49.820
How do you do, Successor of Astral.

00:08:50.790 --> 00:08:52.920
My name is Li Seiou.

00:08:53.060 --> 00:08:56.090
You... What have you done to Kuroha?!

00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:59.260
I've simply immobilized
her a bit with a talisman.

00:08:59.470 --> 00:09:02.560
It's painful, I'm sure, but it won't destroy her.

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:06.670
Besides, the caterpillar fungus
was originally my fetish.

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:07.310
Huh?

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:11.670
Didn't Diana from Trismegistos mention that?

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:15.980
10 years ago, Diana and you people from Astral...

00:09:15.980 --> 00:09:19.040
...stole that caterpillar fungus
seedling from me and hid it here.

00:09:19.220 --> 00:09:21.590
Stole? Dad and Diana did?

00:09:21.690 --> 00:09:24.060
Not to mention casting a
barrier around this area...

00:09:24.060 --> 00:09:26.650
...to keep people from getting near.

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:27.930
However...

00:09:29.530 --> 00:09:31.760
Tonight, that barrier collapsed.

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:37.940
Yes, when the caterpillar fungus blooms,
it destroys every sort of barrier.

00:09:37.940 --> 00:09:40.980
Just that. Such is the great
power that flower possesses.

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:44.540
I'm taking the flower, as is my right.

00:09:44.910 --> 00:09:47.880
And that's... that's why you hurt Kuroha?!

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:51.280
I see no reason to show mercy to a thief,
even if they are a dead spirit.

00:09:57.790 --> 00:10:02.090
Kuroha is my employee! Don't insult her!

00:10:02.230 --> 00:10:04.030
Oh, I beg your pardon.

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:06.590
Now then, I'm taking the flower.

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:13.870
Since they cremate the dead in this country,
I can't use the remains directly.

00:10:14.010 --> 00:10:16.810
Even so, this is definitely a graveyard.

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:26.750
What the?!

00:10:27.190 --> 00:10:28.820
I call them paper soldiers.

00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:31.090
They're quickly made and don't last very long,

00:10:31.090 --> 00:10:33.190
but their appetite is quite strong, I assure you.

00:10:33.190 --> 00:10:37.760
The only thing that will fill the stomachs
of the dead is the flesh of the living!

00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:48.940
What's wrong?

00:10:49.010 --> 00:10:53.110
Your previous president was quite formidable,
but is his successor nothing but a coward?

00:11:03.290 --> 00:11:04.590
Boss, this way!

00:11:07.260 --> 00:11:08.060
Kuroha!

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:15.590
Kuroha, try again!

00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:23.570
KUROHA!!!

00:11:23.880 --> 00:11:25.180
Itsuki!

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:35.720
Honami, why didn't you save Kuroha?!

00:11:36.890 --> 00:11:39.160
Looks like this was a trap from the start.

00:11:40.660 --> 00:11:41.590
A trap?

00:11:42.900 --> 00:11:44.360
Hear me, fragile stone.

00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:48.300
Thy weakness lets you know
the flow of the earth.

00:11:48.300 --> 00:11:50.030
Therefore, reveal the flow unto us.

00:11:52.070 --> 00:11:52.800
What's?

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:55.480
It's a rock collected from the
mountain recesses of Wales.

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:57.310
Since it's sensitive to spell power,

00:11:57.310 --> 00:11:59.280
it's good for seeing through camouflage.

00:12:06.720 --> 00:12:10.090
Judging from his methods,
he's probably using Qi Men Du Jia.

00:12:10.420 --> 00:12:13.550
Easy to get in, nearly impossible to get out.

00:12:14.430 --> 00:12:17.470
We can tunnel through the
ground or fly in the air...

00:12:17.470 --> 00:12:19.760
...and still wind up back where he is.

00:12:20.070 --> 00:12:23.900
If you break the spell without being careful,
it'll take most of your spell power.

00:12:25.210 --> 00:12:26.640
I can't see the moon.

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:28.160
That guy really is a wily one.

00:12:28.340 --> 00:12:31.640
He said the caterpillar fungus was his.

00:12:32.110 --> 00:12:34.080
That my father and Diana stole it from him.

00:12:35.280 --> 00:12:38.410
Even if that's true, it's a pretty lame excuse.

00:12:39.050 --> 00:12:42.510
If a magical society has a
fetish stolen, it's its own fault.

00:12:42.890 --> 00:12:48.420
Father... Astral hid the fungus here
and apparently cast a barrier around it.

00:12:49.130 --> 00:12:51.560
But that barrier collapsed tonight.

00:12:51.730 --> 00:12:52.790
I get it.

00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:55.770
Diana knew that, so she asked us to do this.

00:12:58.040 --> 00:12:59.200
This is a memory.

00:12:59.410 --> 00:13:00.240
A memory?

00:13:00.440 --> 00:13:03.810
Life energy is essentially people's memories.

00:13:04.040 --> 00:13:07.050
When people die,
their memories burst out and vanish.

00:13:07.050 --> 00:13:10.570
The difference here is that this flower
absorbs them and gets power from it.

00:13:10.650 --> 00:13:14.450
You mean this flower blooms by absorbing
the memories of a living person?

00:13:14.920 --> 00:13:15.950
Exactly...

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:20.720
Which would make it a very valuable fetish
for a necromancer who controls the dead.

00:13:21.730 --> 00:13:24.990
He could control a thousand
dead people with this.

00:13:25.330 --> 00:13:29.460
That guy in the Taoist get-up back
there would kill for this thing.

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:31.140
What should we do, Boss?

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:34.740
Try and strike a bargain to
exchange the flower for Kuroha?

00:13:34.740 --> 00:13:39.150
He probably wants to avoid a needless
battle, so he'd be open to negotiation.

00:13:41.680 --> 00:13:43.780
I think this is our job.

00:13:44.850 --> 00:13:48.520
I can't allow him to use the dead as his tools!

00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:52.630
I understand perfectly why Diana wants
to get the caterpillar fungus back...

00:13:52.630 --> 00:13:54.150
...from a man like that.

00:13:54.260 --> 00:13:56.750
I think that's why my father took this job.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:01.940
And I think that since my
father accepted this job,

00:14:01.940 --> 00:14:03.840
it's my responsibility now.

00:14:04.540 --> 00:14:09.500
It's Astral's duty to see this job through
and to rescue Kuroha, isn't it?

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:13.040
Even though you're terrified.

00:14:13.650 --> 00:14:15.850
Even though you're a cowardly, thoughtless,

00:14:15.850 --> 00:14:18.510
bleeding-heart, unqualified,
scatterbrained, impulsive goof-off!

00:14:19.020 --> 00:14:20.610
Do you have to be so mean about it?

00:14:21.320 --> 00:14:22.550
Still, I don't mind.

00:14:23.690 --> 00:14:26.990
If the president says it,
the employee has to do it, right?

00:14:27.190 --> 00:14:28.090
Honami...

00:14:29.330 --> 00:14:31.460
I'm getting a bonus for doing this, though.

00:14:31.570 --> 00:14:32.930
Huh? How much?

00:14:33.930 --> 00:14:35.700
Three month's salary.

00:14:35.700 --> 00:14:37.330
HUH?!

00:14:41.310 --> 00:14:42.970
How do you feel?

00:14:48.720 --> 00:14:51.210
One false move and you'll be destroyed.

00:14:51.850 --> 00:14:54.220
I wouldn't talk either, if I were you.

00:14:54.590 --> 00:14:57.280
How... How can you be so cruel?

00:14:57.630 --> 00:14:59.860
You mean my paper soldiers?

00:15:00.130 --> 00:15:02.120
Dead spirits are mindless.

00:15:02.300 --> 00:15:04.060
I don't give it a second thought.

00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:07.570
Oh, excuse me.
You're a dead spirit too, aren't you?

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:10.100
You have sympathy for your compatriots?

00:15:14.880 --> 00:15:18.640
So, you've come all the way to the
Far East to get the caterpillar fungus?

00:15:21.480 --> 00:15:24.280
It's been a long time, Li Seiou.

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:28.290
It's only natural to take back
what was stolen from you!

00:15:28.820 --> 00:15:31.790
Yes. It was most definitely stolen.

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:35.730
I regret to this day selling that seedling to you.

00:15:36.260 --> 00:15:39.600
How many people did you make into
your paper soldiers in that month?

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:43.700
A hundred, at most. Hardly even worth counting.

00:15:43.700 --> 00:15:44.760
A hundred?!

00:15:44.910 --> 00:15:47.070
Yes, it was nothing.

00:15:47.470 --> 00:15:50.440
When I bought the fungus
seedling from this person,

00:15:50.440 --> 00:15:54.380
I simply took the life force
of a village to fertilize it.

00:15:56.450 --> 00:16:00.250
Could that be why you've been wearing
mourning clothes? Ever since?

00:16:00.420 --> 00:16:02.480
How stupid!

00:16:02.690 --> 00:16:07.060
Yes. I've worn mourning clothes
ever since that day.

00:16:07.900 --> 00:16:09.830
That day, 10 years ago...

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:14.570
The Li Seiou who appeared
before me was just a young man,

00:16:14.570 --> 00:16:18.560
burning with passion for
the possibilities magic held.

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:25.210
But that was my miscalculation.

00:16:25.980 --> 00:16:29.520
Li Seiou attacked an innocent village,

00:16:29.520 --> 00:16:34.890
using their lives as nutrients for the caterpillar
fungus to make it bloom even faster.

00:16:40.230 --> 00:16:41.460
If I'd done nothing,

00:16:41.460 --> 00:16:45.490
there's no telling how many he would have
killed and made into his paper soldiers.

00:16:46.130 --> 00:16:50.400
I made a Rental Magica request
from the former head of Astral.

00:16:56.810 --> 00:16:59.310
I had them hide the fungus in this graveyard...

00:16:59.310 --> 00:17:03.370
...and then cast multiple barriers
to keep Seiou away.

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:07.690
Seeing as tonight is when the
caterpillar fungus blooms,

00:17:07.690 --> 00:17:10.120
I knew you'd appear.

00:17:11.590 --> 00:17:15.190
It was foolish to have misjudged you so badly.

00:17:15.600 --> 00:17:18.030
I came here tonight to finish
this once and for all.

00:17:18.230 --> 00:17:20.270
As the head of Trismegistos,

00:17:20.270 --> 00:17:23.460
even if I die with you, this matter will finally end.

00:17:23.570 --> 00:17:26.000
And then what becomes of the fungus?

00:17:26.170 --> 00:17:29.210
Never mind that. I've left it to Astral.

00:17:29.210 --> 00:17:33.770
Tsukasa Iba? The mage who cannot
practice magic is no more!

00:17:34.280 --> 00:17:36.720
Astral is a relic of a bygone age!

00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:37.310
You're wrong!

00:17:38.150 --> 00:17:40.090
Astral is still here!

00:17:40.590 --> 00:17:43.990
Any closer and I turn her into one of my slaves!

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:47.420
Now then, will you return the fungus to me?

00:18:02.540 --> 00:18:03.370
What?!

00:18:04.110 --> 00:18:05.580
Poltergeist?!

00:18:06.950 --> 00:18:07.680
Kuroha!

00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:09.750
Are you okay?

00:18:09.750 --> 00:18:10.310
Yeah.

00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:12.180
Young President.

00:18:13.350 --> 00:18:15.910
Diana, this is Astral's job to do.

00:18:16.090 --> 00:18:17.390
Will you leave this to us?

00:18:20.430 --> 00:18:22.950
You don't have the power to
defeat my paper soldiers!

00:18:23.730 --> 00:18:24.460
Shut up.

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:25.320
Icchan!

00:18:26.100 --> 00:18:28.190
I don't know the method to defeat your soldiers.

00:18:28.640 --> 00:18:30.740
But in the end, it's still magic, isn't it?

00:18:30.740 --> 00:18:33.260
And that's all the same to me!

00:18:35.110 --> 00:18:35.840
That's!

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:37.500
Glam Sight?!

00:18:37.980 --> 00:18:39.170
D-Damn you!

00:18:39.710 --> 00:18:41.540
Go, my paper soldiers!

00:18:59.400 --> 00:19:00.630
Damn you!

00:19:06.270 --> 00:19:06.800
Honami!

00:19:08.610 --> 00:19:09.910
As your president, I order you!

00:19:10.180 --> 00:19:12.870
52 degrees, rightward! 31 degrees, leftward!

00:19:13.110 --> 00:19:14.440
Fire mistletoe arrows!

00:19:14.750 --> 00:19:15.310
Hail!

00:19:15.580 --> 00:19:17.850
By the cone of power, I entreat you!

00:19:17.990 --> 00:19:20.590
With the divine protection of the mistletoe
which dwells in neither heaven nor earth,

00:19:20.590 --> 00:19:22.380
pierce through the calamity in the northeast!

00:19:26.830 --> 00:19:29.760
54 degrees, downward! 81 degrees, leftward!

00:19:29.960 --> 00:19:31.430
Fire mistletoe shot!

00:19:32.600 --> 00:19:33.190
Hail!

00:19:33.470 --> 00:19:36.000
By the blessings of the maiden of
the crescent moon and mistletoe,

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:37.800
smash the calamity in the west!

00:19:46.210 --> 00:19:47.040
Itsuki!

00:19:48.380 --> 00:19:49.820
Kuroha, image!

00:19:54.350 --> 00:19:58.220
Sephirot! Discharge spell power
directly from Malkuth to Kether!

00:20:19.550 --> 00:20:22.570
You shall pay for your arrogance!

00:20:30.620 --> 00:20:31.890
Nice job.

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:33.420
Right.

00:20:40.930 --> 00:20:41.870
Here you go.

00:20:46.370 --> 00:20:47.170
Mother...

00:20:55.280 --> 00:20:56.040
Is that?!

00:20:56.520 --> 00:21:00.780
Bodies which have the trait to
grow a caterpillar fungus are rare.

00:21:01.490 --> 00:21:04.360
My family's genetic line carries that trait.

00:21:04.790 --> 00:21:09.320
Therefore, I've been obliged to act as
a seedbed for one since I was born.

00:21:09.960 --> 00:21:10.620
Then...

00:21:11.130 --> 00:21:14.900
Yes. One day, I too will bloom as a white flower.

00:21:17.700 --> 00:21:19.400
Goodbye then, Diana.

00:21:20.970 --> 00:21:22.500
Young President, that eye...

00:21:22.610 --> 00:21:24.040
W-What about it?

00:21:24.110 --> 00:21:26.380
Stop that. Let me see it.

00:21:26.450 --> 00:21:27.380
S-Sure...

00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:33.650
W-W-What are you?!

00:21:36.990 --> 00:21:38.750
N... No! This is just!

00:21:38.830 --> 00:21:41.350
Right. I was just teasing him a little.

00:21:42.600 --> 00:21:46.730
Call me any time if you need
your eye patch remade.

00:21:46.930 --> 00:21:48.960
I'll give you a good price for the consultation.

00:21:49.400 --> 00:21:52.460
I look forward to doing business
with you, Young President.

00:21:53.410 --> 00:21:54.270
R-Right...

00:21:54.470 --> 00:21:55.440
Well, see you again.

00:21:55.440 --> 00:21:56.640
No, you won't!
No, you won't!

00:21:58.210 --> 00:22:07.810
Over and over, holding my wounded hand...
Kizutsuku te wo nandomo tsunaide

00:22:08.220 --> 00:22:16.220
...you walk this uncertain path with me...
fuan bakari no kono michi wo aruite

00:22:17.500 --> 00:22:29.270
...amidst the days as they slowly drift by.
yukkuri nagareta hibi no naka de bokura ga

00:22:29.540 --> 00:22:41.190
The things we obtain are so warm, so beloved.
Te ni shita mono wa konna ni atatakute itoshinda

00:22:41.190 --> 00:22:47.460
Please, as time goes by, let's keep right on...
Nee konomama toki no naka

00:22:47.530 --> 00:22:51.960
...laughing and walking together.
waratte aruite yukou

00:22:52.830 --> 00:22:56.240
It's because you're with me...
Kimi ga iru kara

00:22:56.240 --> 00:23:01.330
...that I can keep moving forward.
mae ni susumerunda

00:23:02.280 --> 00:23:13.210
Now our feelings are becoming one...
Ima bokura no omoi ga hitotsu ni natte

00:23:13.590 --> 00:23:17.260
...and showing the path to us.
michi wo shimesunda

00:23:17.260 --> 00:23:21.490
So please, keep on holding my hand...
Dakara kono te zutto

00:23:21.600 --> 00:23:24.590
...and never let it go...
hanasanaide

00:23:26.030 --> 00:23:27.000
Paper Soldier [SHIHEl]

00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:29.470
Paper Soldier [SHIHEl]
T-They aren't Kyonshi, are they?

00:23:29.470 --> 00:23:29.940
Paper Soldier [SHIHEl]
Well, same basic principle.

00:23:29.940 --> 00:23:31.270
Well, same basic principle.

00:23:31.270 --> 00:23:34.240
They actually aren't that different
from Nekoyashiki's cats.

00:23:34.240 --> 00:23:35.580
Oh? Really?

00:23:35.580 --> 00:23:37.210
Right! Nekoyashi-

00:23:37.210 --> 00:23:38.550
Gah! Prof. Miwa!

